  READING: as additive energy E(S) RISES (dissociated -> near-AP -> AP), the lonely measure L
  FALLS toward 0 and the Riesz ratio RISES toward 1 -- the quantitative loose/tight law. The AP
  (max E, tight L=0, ratio=1) is the extremal; dissociated (min E) has L~(6/7)^13 & ratio<<1.
